+## jumper.power_backflip
+
+### Reward and termination
+
+The jump spin's construction about the pitch axis, nose up positive, with the
+in-air rate weighted at 15 per rad/s rather than 1: at 5 the policy settled on a hop
+that leans back (below). `landed_turn` 4 per half turn, the same tent at a full turn.
+
+**Terminations changed.** `ref_free_jump`'s 50 degree tilt limit (`fell_over`) is
+removed -- a flip passes through every tilt. In its place:
+
+- `chassis_crash`: any of the five chassis collision geoms (base, upper shell, camera,
+  ToF, display) pressing on the ground over 1 N;
+- `tipped_on_feet`: tilt past 80 degrees while any foot is on the ground.
+
+Time-out and back-at-`HOME` are unchanged. In the air the tilt is unlimited. On the
+robot, `deploy/jumper.controller.toml` drops to `safe` at 50 degrees in every mode, so a
+flip mode would need that guard lifted, and its landings tilt past 50 (below).
+
+Since the handover start the task also takes back in-air turn that did not make a flip
+(`turn_clawback`) and bridges from mjlab's reset for its first 900 iterations; the runs
+below came before both ("The handover start").
