+## Under the controller
+
+The `crabcraft` bundle (`deploy/crabcraft.manifests.json`) carries the spin as
+`power_spin`, on Home + LB on the pad and Shift + 5 on the keyboard, from locomotion (and,
+since the handover start, the two jumps: "In the bundle"). It
+has no recording and no clock, so nothing ends it but its switch pressed again or Menu
+(Ctrl) on its own. Through the bundle's controller, entered from walking after the
+switch-in ramp: 2.06 rev/s over the last 2 s of 3.5 s held, 2632 degrees from the policy's
+first tick to walking again, tilt at most 7.9 degrees (crabcraft's
+`tools/motion/record_clips.py`, its MuJoCo host on the training contact model); 2.02 rev/s
+over 4 s held, tilt at most 8.1 degrees, on the browser's MuJoCo build (crabcraft's
+`tools/robot-sim-check.ts`). Both are slower than the 2.33 rev/s of its own environment: the
+controller clamped its joint targets at the stops, and with its targets let past them it runs
+2.33 ("The controller gap"). Let go, the controller's ramp stands it up and hands back to
+walking within 1.1 s.
+
+**Until the handover start, the two jumps took off only from their training
+environment's reset.** Their actor sees no clock and no command, so what starts the jump
+has to be in what it does see, and in training every episode began at mjlab's reset,
+whose first observation shows `joint_torque` at the servo's limit, 1.746 N*m, on 18 of the
+20 joints, in all five frames of the history: the actuator's PD toward a target of zero
+before the first action, saturated by `HOME`'s offsets (the other two, the middle legs'
+`J0`, sit 0.0012 rad from zero and read 0.024). A controller switching into the
+mode hands the policy a robot standing at `HOME` with its real torques. Measured in each
+task's own environment (native:cpu, play mode, DR off): with the robot held at `HOME` by
+zero actions for 0.5 s and then handed to the policy, `pw-jspin720` lifted its base 9 mm
+and turned 18 degrees in 2.5 s, `pw-flip-T` lifted it 0 mm and turned 0; handed over at
+the reset itself, as trained, they rose 268 mm and turned 805, and rose 215 mm and turned
+362 about pitch. The spin is indifferent: 1996 degrees in 2.5 s after a 0.5 s hold, 2038
+without one. Through the bundle's controller `pw-jspin720` rose 10 mm in 2.6 s; with the
+reset's torque frames written into its first observations by hand (a diagnosis, not
+something shipped) it rose 215 mm.
