+**The flip at rest, and after it.** It comes to rest on its rear and middle legs swung back, the
+largest gait-joint distance from `HOME` 0.54 to 0.56 rad (`LR_J0`, `RR_J0`), 0.34 rad RMS, 7.2
+to 7.7 degrees nose-down. Its switch pressed at 1.2 s, the ramp takes the joints to
+locomotion's `HOME`: when the walking policy runs again, 0.855 s after the press, the body is 1.4
+degrees nose-down and every gait joint within 0.10 rad of `HOME`. 1.5 s after the press,
+standing, it is 0.6 to 1.6 degrees from level with its largest joint 0.16 to 0.23 rad from
+`HOME`, which is how locomotion stands on its own (0.06 degrees and 0.21 rad, 5 s after the
+keyframe); walking at 0.28 m/s from the press, 0.4 degrees nose-down and 0.25 rad, inside the
+gait's own range (1.7 degrees nose-down to 0.4 nose-up, 0.15 to 0.46 rad). So the hand-back
+brings the splayed landing pose level; nothing in the flip's own mode does. The 720 comes to rest
+1.8 to 2.2 degrees nose-down, its largest joint 0.28 rad from `HOME` (`RM_J0`), 0.13 rad RMS.
+Without `skip_tilt_check` the settled flip still goes to `safe` at the top (4 of 4 from
+standing), so the lift stays.
+
+**No `target_margin` for the flip.** Clamped, it already flies as in its environment: 392
+degrees against 392, 0.193 m of lowest-point rise against 0.196. Given the 720's 1.7 rad for the
+measurement (written into its state, not shipped), 12 trials each: 390 (389 to 393) degrees from
+standing and 393 (389 to 398) from walking, 0.214 and 0.201 m of base rise, 1.1 to 1.6 cm more;
+and a second flight over 1 cm after 20 of the 24 landings, up to 4.7 cm, against 3 and 1.3 cm
+clamped, at rest at 0.82 s rather than 0.79. Its targets would lie past a stop in 9.3 to 10.1% of
+the steps over the 1.5 s after the handover (39 to 42% of the push's), and a joint would be held
+against its stop in 1.6 to 2.0% of the joint-steps, at a median 1.746 N*m. It turns no further and
+lands worse, so it stays clamped.
