+**The 720's margin, through this bundle.** Over the 1.5 s after the handover 16.5 to 18.7% of
+its targets lie past a stop: 36 to 39% of the push's, 29 to 37% of the flight's, at most 0.7% of
+those in the 0.3 s after the touchdown and none after. A joint sits within 0.02 rad of a stop with
+its target past it in 6.2 to 7.4% of the joint-steps, at a median 1.2 N*m, and in none after 1.0
+s. The largest target it sends is 4.45 rad; the bound is 6.45, the shoulders' -4.75 stop less
+1.7. What that costs on a robot is "What it costs on a robot".
+
+**Robot Mode's presses.** At rest by 1.14 s (720) and 0.86 s (flip) after the handover, the jumps
+are 0.26 s and 0.34 s at rest when Robot Mode presses their switch at 1.4 s and 1.2 s. On
+crabcraft's browser core (`src/robot/sim/core.ts` under Node, MuJoCo WASM, the bundle's
+`controller.wasm`, onnxruntime-web; 12 trials each from standing and walking, the host's own press
+turned off and made at 3.7 s): the 720 turned 690 to 746 degrees at 0.36 to 0.40 m and was at rest
+0.99 to 1.12 s after the handover, the flip 381 to 395 at 0.18 to 0.20 m and at rest 0.69 to 0.83
+s, every trial upright and none in `safe`. Both delays stay.
+
+## Found along the way
+
+**Non-foot parts are not frictionless against the floor.** `common/constants.py` gives
+every geom but the six feet condim 1. Their priority equals the ground plane's, so
+MuJoCo combines each pair -- the larger condim, the larger friction -- and a calf or a
+palm on the floor is condim 3 at friction 1.0, the plane's. Measured on `pw-spin-a`'s
+`model_399` (native:cpu, DR off): every calf and palm contact was (3, 1.0). The feet
+carry priority 1, so their own friction (and its randomisation) is what applies.
+
+**warp and native disagree about those contacts.** The same checkpoint
+(`pw-spin-c20`'s `model_399`, DR off, 3 s, one environment) had a non-foot part on
+the ground over 1 N in 44.6% of steps on `native:cpu` and 3.0% on `warp:cpu`, spinning at
+1.79 and 1.87 rev/s. The calf geometry dips below the floor on both (left-middle calf's
+lowest hull vertex at its 1st percentile: -7.8 mm native, -6.6 mm warp), so the
+difference is in the force the contact produces, not in whether the leg reaches the
+floor. Every policy here trained on warp; every number in the tables is native's.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+On the cluster, one H100, `warp:cuda`, 4096 environments. `train_power.sbatch` is
+`~/crabcraft-train/train_task.sbatch` with the checkout to train from put first on
+`PYTHONPATH` (the shared venv's editable install points at another clone) and its
+`tasks` and `mjlab` import paths printed in the header:
+
+```bash
+sbatch -J pw-spin  ~/crabcraft-train/power/train_power.sbatch jumper.power_spin 3000
+sbatch -J pw-jspin ~/crabcraft-train/power/train_power.sbatch jumper.power_jumpspin 4000
+sbatch -J pw-flip  ~/crabcraft-train/power/train_power.sbatch jumper.power_backflip 2500
+```
+
+These are the budgets the runs above add up to; the runs themselves came in stages, each
+resumed from the last (`--checkpoint`), and the earlier stages trained on the commits in
+the tables, not this one. The handover start's runs resumed the shipped checkpoints from
+before it, with `train_dance.sbatch` (the same script, another checkout):
+
+```bash
+R=~/crabcraft-train/runs
+sbatch -J pw-jspin720-ho ~/crabcraft-train/dance/train_dance.sbatch jumper.power_jumpspin720 2000 4096 pw-jspin720-ho \
+    --checkpoint $R/pw-jspin720/logs/jumper/jumper.power_jumpspin/2026-10-15_14-29-33/model_3997.pt
+sbatch -J pw-flip-brc ~/crabcraft-train/dance/train_dance.sbatch jumper.power_backflip 1500 4096 pw-flip-brc \
+    --checkpoint $R/pw-flip-T/logs/jumper/jumper.power_backflip/2026-10-15_13-54-57/model_2498.pt
+```
+The settled jumps resumed the shipped checkpoints with their action noise capped
+(`tools/cap_noise.py`), the 720 on CORE
+and the flip on `legion` after 953 iterations on CORE:
+
+```bash
+python tools/cap_noise.py pw-jspin720-ho/model_5996.pt j720_ho_5996_std015.pt 0.15
+python tools/cap_noise.py pw-flip-brc/model_3997.pt flip_brc_3997_std015.pt 0.15
