@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+"""jumper.break_oneclaw -- a one-claw freeze, a keyframed reference learned by imitation.
+
+One of the breaking moves for "World of Crabcraft", on the dance machinery as the
+crabcraft skills are: the environment is `tasks/jumper/common/dance/env.py`, and what
+this directory adds is the clip and the numbers.
+
+## The clip
+
+`media/oneclaw.npz`, written by `tools/author_breaking_clips.py`, whose docstring has
+how the clip is made and checked; `docs/CRABCRAFT_BREAKING.md` has the numbers it
+passed with.
+
+The claw stand with the right claw up: two bounces on the beat while the body
+moves 50 mm towards the claws, then the nose goes down 34 degrees, the rear legs
+swing up and out and the right claw rises high and open, hitting the freeze on
+the fourth beat (2.24 s); held 1.68 s on three points, the left claw and the
+middle feet, then back the same way, the right claw landing 0.36 s after the
+rear feet, once the nose is up far enough for its wrist.
+
+The clip begins at `HOME` and ends with a lead-out back to it and half a second
+standing there, 6.52 s in all, so it starts and ends where the walking policy
+stands. The game plays a window of it: down from 1.68 s, the freeze 2.24 to 3.92 s,
+recovered by 5.60 s.
+
+There is no music, and nothing to export a performance video with: export with
+`--no-video`.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+from ...registry import register
+from ..common.assets import JUMPER_ASSETS
+
+register(
+    id="jumper.break_oneclaw",
+    assets=JUMPER_ASSETS,
+    description="jumper hexapod imitating a breaking freeze on one claw; the clip is "
+                "committed in tasks/jumper/break_oneclaw/media/",
+    tags=("imitation", "jumper", "breaking", "flat"),
+)
