+"""jumper.skill_cast -- crabcraft's spell cast, a keyframed reference learned by imitation.
+
+A one-shot move on the dance machinery, as the gestures are: the environment is
+`tasks/jumper/common/dance/env.py`, and what this directory adds is the clip and
+the numbers.
+
+## The clip
+
+`media/cast.npz`, written by `tools/author_skill_clips.py`, whose docstring has how
+the clip is made and checked; `docs/CRABCRAFT_SKILLS.md` has the numbers it passed
+with. It replaces `cast`, one of the hand keyframes "World of Crabcraft" played
+where every other move is a rollout of a trained policy.
+
+The robot rocks 40 mm back so both claws can lift, gathers them under the
+visor, rises on straightened legs with the claws raised and parted, holds them
+there through two flourishes of the wrists and pincers, flings them up and wide
+on the release, and sets them down again before the body comes forward. The
+channel, 1.00 to 2.20 s, starts and ends on the same pose, so the game can
+loop it for as long as a cast bar runs.
+
+The clip begins at `HOME` and ends with a lead-out back to it and half a second
+standing there, 4.86 s in all, so it starts and ends where the walking policy
+stands. The game plays a window of it: gather 0.68 s, channel 1.00 to 2.20 s,
+release 2.40 s, recovered 3.10 s.
+
+There is no music, and nothing to export a performance video with: export with
+`--no-video`.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+from ...registry import register
+from ..common.assets import JUMPER_ASSETS
+
+register(
+    id="jumper.skill_cast",
+    assets=JUMPER_ASSETS,
+    description="jumper hexapod imitating crabcraft's spell cast; the clip is "
+                "committed in tasks/jumper/skill_cast/media/",
+    tags=("imitation", "jumper", "skill", "flat"),
+)
