@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+"""jumper.skill_flinch -- a flinch from a hit, a keyframed reference learned by imitation.
+
+A one-shot move on the dance machinery, as the gestures are: the environment is
+`tasks/jumper/common/dance/env.py`, and what this directory adds is the clip and
+the numbers.
+
+## The clip
+
+`media/flinch.npz`, written by `tools/author_skill_clips.py`, whose docstring has how
+the clip is made and checked; `docs/CRABCRAFT_SKILLS.md` has the numbers it passed
+with. It replaces `hit_react`, one of the hand keyframes "World of Crabcraft" played
+where every other move is a rollout of a trained policy.
+
+Struck from the front, the shell jolts 16 mm back and nose-up with a little
+roll and twist while the left claw snaps up across the visor; it rebounds a
+little past rest and the claw comes back down. One claw, not two: with the
+right one on the floor the jolt does not have to carry the centre of mass
+40 mm back first. 0.46 s is the fastest this move can be balanced at with the
+feet at friction 0.5, where the game's keyframes took 0.5 s;
+`docs/CRABCRAFT_SKILLS.md` has the scan.
+
+The clip begins at `HOME` and ends with a lead-out back to it and half a second
+standing there, 1.38 s in all, so it starts and ends where the walking policy
+stands. The game plays a window of it: hit 0.00 s, recoil 0.16 s, recovered 0.46 s.
+
+There is no music, and nothing to export a performance video with: export with
+`--no-video`.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+from ...registry import register
+from ..common.assets import JUMPER_ASSETS
+
+register(
+    id="jumper.skill_flinch",
+    assets=JUMPER_ASSETS,
+    description="jumper hexapod imitating crabcraft's flinch from a hit; the clip is "
+                "committed in tasks/jumper/skill_flinch/media/",
+    tags=("imitation", "jumper", "skill", "flat"),
+)
