+"""jumper.skill_slam -- crabcraft's two-claw slam, a keyframed reference learned by imitation.
+
+A one-shot move on the dance machinery, as the gestures are: the environment is
+`tasks/jumper/common/dance/env.py`, and what this directory adds is the clip and
+the numbers.
+
+## The clip
+
+`media/slam.npz`, written by `tools/author_skill_clips.py`, whose docstring has how
+the clip is made and checked; `docs/CRABCRAFT_SKILLS.md` has the numbers it passed
+with. It replaces `attack_slam`, one of the hand keyframes "World of Crabcraft" played
+where every other move is a rollout of a trained policy.
+
+The robot rocks 40 mm back onto its middle and rear legs, which is what lets
+both claws leave the floor (the centre of mass sits ahead of the middle
+feet), rears up with both claws high and open, and brings them down onto the
+floor in front, the shell pitching nose-down into the impact. The claws step
+forward to where they stand at `HOME` before the body comes forward.
+
+The clip begins at `HOME` and ends with a lead-out back to it and half a second
+standing there, 3.38 s in all, so it starts and ends where the walking policy
+stands. The game plays a window of it: windup 0.90 s, hit 1.12 s, recovered 1.50 s.
+
+There is no music, and nothing to export a performance video with: export with
+`--no-video`.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+from ...registry import register
+from ..common.assets import JUMPER_ASSETS
+
+register(
+    id="jumper.skill_slam",
+    assets=JUMPER_ASSETS,
+    description="jumper hexapod imitating crabcraft's two-claw slam; the clip is "
+                "committed in tasks/jumper/skill_slam/media/",
+    tags=("imitation", "jumper", "skill", "flat"),
+)
